// KERNEL=aievec static gate (check_aievec_core.py): .text budget, exact
// commit / MMAC / pop / insert (and OUT=i8 vst.srs) counts, one crRnd /
// crSat write, no lda.s8 or vector stack traffic, no post-incremented
// staging index, and the zb/za timing check around each K-loop of core
// (0,2). Config A is #358's lit size (OUT=i8); config C (OUT=i32) with
// trace events is the largest core. Config B (K = 128) has no K-loop (it is
// inlined) and Peano spills accumulators there, so vector stack traffic is
// allowed and its timing is covered by hardware only.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// The default AIEVEC_LLC_ARGS software-pipeline both K-loops of a core:
// each adds one K-tile copy (prologue/epilogue) to the exact counts, and
// the timing check covers the straight-line block around each K-loop
// (entry, two iterations, exit and the peeled last K-tile).
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_aievec_codegen
// RUN: cd test_aievec_codegen
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check_aievec KERNEL=aievec M=512 N=768 K=1024 OUT=i8 CT=4 ITERS=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,I8
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check_aievec KERNEL=aievec M=512 N=576 K=256 OUT=i32 CT=1 ITERS=2 TRACE_SIZE=8192 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,I32
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check_aievec KERNEL=aievec M=512 N=576 K=128 OUT=i8 CT=1 ITERS=2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KT2
// I8: core_0_2: {{.*}} commit 6 mmac 384 pop 192 insert 192 {{.*}} vst.srs 128 crrnd 1 crsat 1; {{.*}}; 2 pipelined
// I32: core_0_2: {{.*}} commit 6 mmac 384 pop 192 insert 192 {{.*}}; 2 pipelined
// I8: core_0_2 K-loop {{.*}}: ORDER OK: 5 tiles, 128 inserts, 256 MMACs, no accumulator spills (loop body checked twice)
// I32: core_0_2 K-loop {{.*}}: ORDER OK: 5 tiles, 160 inserts, 256 MMACs, no accumulator spills (loop body checked twice)
// CHECK: core_0_2 K-loop {{.*}}: ORDER OK: 5 tiles, 96 inserts, 256 MMACs, no accumulator spills (loop body checked twice)
// CHECK: CHECK_AIEVEC OK: 12 cores
// KT2: core_0_2: {{.*}} vst.srs 128 crrnd 1 crsat 1 (vector [sp {{[0-9]+}}, allowed); ZOLs 1; no K-loop
// KT2: CHECK_AIEVEC OK: 12 cores
